    {
      "id": "2ha573m",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>EXAM KEY — Purandaradasa:</strong></p><p>• Born: 1484 at Tirthahalli (Shivamogga)</p><p>• Called 'Pitamaha (Father/Grandfather) of Carnatic Music'</p><p>• Composed over 4,75,000 kirtanas (songs)</p><p>• Introduced Mayamalavagowla raga as the beginners' raga</p><p>• His compositions form the basis of Karnataka Sangita (Carnatic music) curriculum</p><p>• Both Purandaradasa and Kanakadasa were disciples of saint Vyasatirtha (Vijayanagara period)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "id6om4x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.3 Kannada Literature — Epochs"
    },
    {
      "id": "klhu9ky",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Period</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Name / Features</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Works &amp; Authors</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Halegannada (Old Kannada) — 450–1200 CE</p>",
            "<p>Early inscriptional &amp; literary Kannada; Jain influence</p>",
            "<p>Kavirajamarga (850 CE) by Nripatunga — oldest Kannada literary text; Pampa (Vikramarjuna Vijaya), Ponna, Ranna — 'Three Gems of Kannada'</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nadugannada (Middle Kannada) — 1200–1700 CE</p>",
            "<p>Vachana literature; Veerashaiva movement; Vijayanagara period</p>",
            "<p>Basavanna's Vachanas; Allama Prabhu; Akka Mahadevi; Harihara, Raghavanka; Kumara Vyasa</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hosagannada (Modern Kannada) — 1700–present</p>",
            "<p>Western influence; prose; novels; Navodaya-Navya-Bandaya movements</p>",
            "<p>Navodaya: Kuvempu, D. V. Gundappa, Masti; Navya: U. R. Ananthamurthy; Bandaya (protest): Siddalingaiah</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vachana Movement — 12th century</p>",
            "<p>Democratic, anti-caste, devotional poetry in prose</p>",
            "<p>Basavanna, Akka Mahadevi, Allama Prabhu; 'Anubhava Mantapa' — world's first democratic philosophical forum</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Haridasa Movement — 15th–16th century</p>",
            "<p>Devotional compositions in simple Kannada; anti-caste</p>",
            "<p>Purandaradasa, Kanakadasa, Vyasatirtha; Kanakadasa allowed into Udupi temple (Kanakana Kindi story)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
